        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Direct Answer"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Metformin remains the traditional first-line therapy for type 2 diabetes, while SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1 receptor agonists are typically recommended as second-line options\u2014unless a patient has high-risk cardiovascular disease, heart failure, or chronic kidney disease, where guidelines increasingly support starting them early or alongside metformin. Neither class has universally replaced metformin as the default first-line pill for everyone due to cost and access factors, though they offer superior organ-protective benefits.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1 receptor agonists are typically recommended as second-line options"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
